October 6th, 1774

No word from the eastern lookout yet. That either means good news or they're already gone.

Mongo’s been on edge — more than usual. He keeps looking up at the sky like he expects something to fall from it.
Bart says he had a dream about vultures circling the church steeple.

I told them dreams don’t mean much out here, but I’ll admit: I’ve started sleeping with one eye open.

The silence before a storm always feels too clean.

- Jim “The Waco Kid”
